    "windows_exe": [
      "Acrobat.exe",
      "AcroRd32.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.adobe.Acrobat.Pro",
      "com.adobe.Reader"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://helpx.adobe.com/acrobat/using/keyboard-shortcuts.html",
    "https://helpx.adobe.com/acrobat/desktop/get-started/preferences-and-settings/keyboard-shortcuts.html"
  ],
  "note": "Covers Acrobat on desktop (Reader and Pro), current version as of the Sep 23, 2025 update to Adobe's page (helpx.adobe.com/acrobat/using/keyboard-shortcuts.html redirects to the desktop keyboard-shortcuts article). Where the vendor lists two interchangeable keys for one action (e.g. 'Spacebar or Enter', 'Home or Shift+Ctrl+Home'), only the first-listed key is recorded here; the alternate performs the same action. '~' (Open Output Preview) is recorded as the backtick key since '~' itself is not an expressible key in this grammar. Skipped as not expressible: the Dynamic Zoom and temporary-Zoom-out tool selections (a bare Shift/Ctrl/Option modifier with no key), 'control+click' to open a context menu on macOS (mouse), and the numpad-specific 'Enter (keypad)' form-field shortcut. The Windows/macOS terminology-equivalents table at the end of the page (Alt=Option, This PC=[disk name], etc.) is not a shortcut list and is not included.",
